  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> be a twice differentiable function defined on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>''</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math> lies in the interval",
    "image": null
  },
